## Convert date to timestamp

To convert a date to a timestamp, use the date component `timestamp` as shown below:

::: {#ff8e481c .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(df
 .with_columns(DOB_ms=pl.col('DOB').dt.timestamp('ms'))
 )
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (1, 3)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>DOB</th><th>DOB_ms</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>date</td><td>i64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Joram Mutenge&quot;</td><td>2020-07-13</td><td>1594598400000</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


